  "biobricks:reviewed": false,
  "biobricks:reviewNotes": "Determined by the annotation agent (Claude licensing-provenance annotator). The brick combines two upstream sources. WikiPathways data is, to the annotator's knowledge, dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 (medium confidence - the wikipathways.org/license page returned HTTP 403 and could not be quoted directly). The primary EU-ToxRisk TempO-Seq gene-expression data is pulled from a Douglas Connect / EdelweissData development API and carries NO license statement in the repository or any reachable source page. Because the most-restrictive component governs and the EU-ToxRisk license is undetermined, the dataset as a whole is classed 'unknown', and commercial use is marked 'prohibited' as the conservative contract-facing verdict for unstated redistribution rights. HUMAN CHECK REQUIRED: establish the actual license/terms for the EU-ToxRisk TempO-Seq data on EdelweissData (EU-ToxRisk was an EU H2020 project, id 681002) and confirm WikiPathways CC0; if EU-ToxRisk turns out to be openly/attribution licensed the class could be raised.",
